787	   787	    /// per-case HrExecutiveUserMasterId/PayrollExecutiveUserMasterId/FinanceExecutiveUserMasterId/
788	   788	    /// ApproverUserMasterId planning fields, but they are UserMasterIds (not EmployeeMasterIds) and
789	   789	    /// are purely informational today - nothing reads them for authorization, and wiring them into
790	   790	    /// the engine would need a UserMasterId -> EmployeeMasterId resolution this migration does not
791	   791	    /// add. Expected initial setup: `any_one` with the actual Finance/HR/Payroll employee(s) who
792	   792	    /// sign off F&amp;F cases configured explicitly as HR_ApprovalConfigApprover rows - or
793	   793	    /// `default_chain` (IsReportingMgrRequired=true) if the policy is "the exiting employee's
794	   794	    /// manager approves it" instead (HR_FNFSettlement.ReportingPersonId is available for this).
795	   795	    /// Which is correct is a real policy decision, not something inferable from legacy code, since
796	   796	    /// none existed.
